WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.950
Hear a few seconds of Vivaldi's Winter on the radio, and you know at once: this is old music.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.750
Not a few decades old.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.870
Three hundred years old.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.790
Nobody has to tell you the date, or who wrote it.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.150
Yet something in the sound says: old.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.230
What is it?

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.490
What makes Winter sound three hundred years old?

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:30.210
In this mission, you'll follow the finale: a walk on the ice, a slip and a fall, the ice cracking, and every wind at war.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:37.590
Then you'll put Winter beside a concerto by Mozart, written decades later, and spot what he kept and what he dropped.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.950
Your mission: work out what makes Winter sound three hundred years old.
